+Aegis AI platform — Executive Summary (one page)
+
+What it is
+- Aegis AI platform is a secure, auditable AI platform that builds, runs, and governs machine learning models across clouds and edge devices. It provides end‑to‑end model lifecycle automation (ingest → train → sign → deploy → monitor → retrain), enforces policy and human‑in‑the‑loop controls, and produces non‑repudiable evidence for compliance and audits.
+
+Key benefits for customers
+- Trust & compliance: Cosign/Rekor attestations + Vault Transit signing + evidence bundles produce provable lineage and forensics for regulators and legal review.
+- Privacy & safety: Federated learning orchestration, secure aggregation guidance, and Differential Privacy examples enable privacy‑preserving improvement without centralizing raw customer data.
+- Controlled production: Gatekeeper policies, pre‑load attestation checks, and HIL approvals reduce risk of automated missteps and enforce enterprise policies.
+- Cross‑cloud + Edge delivery: Works across clouds and on appliances; supports BYOK/KMS key management, offline fetchtoken flows and local inference.
+- Operational efficiency: CI/CD templates, signed model promotion, monitoring + SLOs reduce mean time to deploy and operate ML features.
+
+Core components (evidence)
+- CI/CD signing flow: OIDC → Vault (OIDC role) → receipt_signer (Vault Transit) → optional Rekor publish
+- Evidence bundles: MLflow-aware bundles attached to artifacts for audit
+- Serving enforcement: pre‑load attestation webhook and Gatekeeper enforcement patterns
+- HIL: A2A/HIL enforcer + Prefilled HIL UI and signed receipts
+- Federated starter: Orchestrator stubs, client SDK, DP example scripts for pilot experimentation
+- Observability: Prometheus/Grafana skeletons, SLO reporter, runbooks
+
+Proof points (pilot acceptance)
+- Attestation coverage: >=95% of promoted models are signed and have evidence bundles in staging
+- Signer latency: median signer roundtrip < 5s in staging
+- Enforcement: pre‑load webhook blocks unsigned loads; Gatekeeper dry‑run completed for 48–72h
+- Privacy: federated pilot documents epsilon/delta and demonstrates utility uplift vs baseline
+
+Suggested next steps (executive / product)
+1. Run two priority pilots: (a) Signed-model & enforcement (8 weeks) and (b) Federated personalization with DP (12 weeks).  
+2. Productionize Vault (HA + KMS/BYOK auto‑unseal) and Rekor (TLS + durable Postgres + backups).  
+3. Complete security hardening (SCA, pentest, secrets elimination in CI).
+
+Contact
+- For technical details, runbooks, and patch artifacts, see the repo docs or contact the Aegis engineering lead.
+
